<div id="2026-11-06-consignment-loop" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-06 — the refill track is now followable on screen</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Applying a count now redirects to the replacement batch it just created, not back to the count screen. The batch page carries a "Why this batch exists" panel: the count that sold the stock (number, text, read/applied times), the invoice it billed (number, total, status, link to the sale), and the print jobs queued for it. The consignment list defaults to <em>open</em> batches with settled ones behind the status filter. Inventory and Accounting dashboards gained a <em>Needs Refill</em> tile counting open batches. Print-queue rows now show a <code>↩ Co-op batch #N</code> link back to the batch they refill.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> The chain photo → count → invoice → replacement → print existed in the data and on no screen. Apply landed on the count screen, so the new batch was only findable by hunting a list that grows forever, and the queue never said which batch a job belonged to.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Anchor.</strong> The invoice, not the photo — every sale, consignment or direct, updates stock and bills from one document. A batch resolves its invoice through the count that created it (<code>inventory_location_counts.invoice_id</code>), so both tracks point at the same document without a schema change. The photo is evidence for the read and is still deleted at apply.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Bug found while testing.</strong> <code>consignment_view</code>'s <code>prefetch => ['partner', { 'lines' => 'item' }]</code> dies with <code>relname_to_table_alias on an undefined value</code>, which turned every visit into "Consignment not found". The action now falls back to a plain <code>find</code> and loads the lines separately.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Verified.</strong> Apply inside a rolled-back transaction: consignment created, redirect target resolved to its view id, source count found by <code>consignment_id</code>, invoice <code>INV-3D-0002</code> resolved at 1.78 draft, one queued job attached, default list filter returned the open batches. <code>view.tt</code> rendered 16,603 bytes with the origin panel present. All 2,015 templates re-parsed; none of the edited files are among the 20 pre-existing failures.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Still open.</strong> <code>inventory_consignments.invoice_id</code> so a batch cites its invoice directly (needs an Update Table), and extracting the shared restock section so a direct sale runs the same code as a consignment refill.</p>
</div>
